{"slug":"find-the-index-of-the-first-occurrence-in-a-string","title":"Find the Index of the First Occurrence in a String","level":"Easy","summary":"Return the index of the first occurrence of needle in haystack, or -1.","method":"strStr","params":[["String","haystack"],["String","needle"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"sadbutsad\"","\"sad\""],"out":"0"},{"in":["\"leetcode\"","\"leeto\""],"out":"-1"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"0"},{"in":["\"mississippi\"","\"issip\""],"out":"4"},{"in":["\"aaaaab\"","\"aab\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aaaaa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bcc\"","\"cc\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aabaaabbaabbbaaaaabaaa\"","\"aba\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"cb\"","\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\"","\"b\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"baa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"a\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"ccacaac\"","\"caabab\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"a\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aa\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"b\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbb\"","\"aa\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaa\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbaaabaaab\"","\"bbbbbb\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\"","\"bbbbbbbb\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaa\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bcaccaaba\"","\"bca\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bbabbca\"","\"bca\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"ccaccaac\"","\"c\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"aaaaa\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbb\"","\"bbb\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"ccccccccc\"","\"cc\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"b\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\"","\"ab\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"a\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbababaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"baabaaaababbbbbbabbbbaaabbaba\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\"","\"bab\""],"out":"0","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"bab\""],"out":"-1","g":1}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"Return the index of the first place where `needle` occurs as a substring of `haystack`, or `-1` if it does not occur at all.\n\nTry to write the search yourself instead of calling `indexOf`.\n\nA simple check at every start position is O(n·m). KMP or a rolling hash brings it down to O(n + m).","constraints":["1 <= haystack.length, needle.length <= 1e4","Both strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["The simple approach tries every start position and compares character by character: O(n · m).","KMP avoids re-reading text: precompute for the needle the length of the longest proper prefix that is also a suffix, for every prefix.","When a mismatch happens, fall back in the needle using that table instead of moving the text pointer back. That is O(n + m)."],"explain":"\"sad\" occurs at index 0 and again at index 6. The first occurrence is at index 0, so the answer is 0."},
{"slug":"rotate-string","title":"Rotate String","level":"Easy","summary":"Return whether s can become goal by repeatedly moving its first character to the end.","method":"rotateString","params":[["String","s"],["String","goal"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["\"abcde\"","\"cdeab\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"abcde\"","\"abced\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"a\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"abab\"","\"baba\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbb\"","\"bbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbab\"","\"bbab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"acbacccbba\"","\"acbacccbbaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\"","\"bb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baa\"","\"aab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbb\"","\"bbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"a\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bccaccbbc\"","\"abbabbaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bba\"","\"bb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbccbba\"","\"bbbbbccbbaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"b\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbbbb\"","\"bbbbabb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abaaabb\"","\"babaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baabaab\"","\"baabba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"b\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bcb\"","\"bab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\"","\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"baaa\"","\"baaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\"","\"bab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abbcaccbcbacbb\"","\"bbbababaabbaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abcaa\"","\"abcaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"cabacccca\"","\"abacccca\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"abab\"","\"abab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abaaa\"","\"aaabb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"ba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"acaab\"","\"aaabb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"c\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"b\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"babba\"","\"babba\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"bba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"aaaaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bacaaabbbb\"","\"bacaaabbbba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\"","\"bb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbb\"","\"bbbbbbbbbba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbaa\"","\"bbaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\"","\"ababaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aab\"","\"aab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aabaaab\"","\"aabaaaba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"abba\"","\"abba\""],"out":"true","g":1}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"A shift moves the first character of `s` to the end, so `\"abcde\"` becomes `\"bcdea\"`. Return `true` if `s` can become `goal` after some number of shifts (including zero).\n\nA neat test: `goal` is a rotation of `s` exactly when the two have the same length and `goal` appears inside `s + s`.","constraints":["1 <= s.length, goal.length <= 100","Both strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Write s twice in a row. Every rotation of s appears inside that doubled string.","So goal is a rotation of s exactly when the lengths are equal and goal is a substring of s + s.","The length check matters: \"a\" is a substring of \"aaaa\" but not a rotation of \"aa\"."],"explain":"Two shifts turn \"abcde\" into \"bcdea\" and then \"cdeab\", which is `goal`. So the answer is `true`."},
{"slug":"repeated-substring-pattern","title":"Repeated Substring Pattern","level":"Easy","summary":"Return whether s can be built by repeating one of its substrings two or more times.","method":"repeatedSubstringPattern","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["\"abab\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"aba\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"abcabcabcabc\""],"out":"true"},{"in":["\"a\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"aabaaba\""],"out":"false"},{"in":["\"aaaaab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ccccabcbc\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"cabbba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"accbcaacaabbcbacacccaaabbbacbc\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"b\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baaab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbabba\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"c\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"acaacaacaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bababababab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ababababababababab\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbcbbbcabbc\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"babababab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"acacabcabcacabcacbcabbcac\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aababaab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baaaccaacabbbbccacc\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bababababababababababab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"cc\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbcaabcaccbacbcbaacaabacccb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"aababbb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbb\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"babaaababab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bcab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aabb\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"bba\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"baabaab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\""],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbaa\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\""],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["\"baaabaaabaaabaaabaa\""],"out":"false","g":1}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"Return `true` if `s` can be built by taking one of its substrings and repeating it two or more times, as `\"abab\"` = `\"ab\"` + `\"ab\"`.\n\nFor contrast, `\"aba\"` cannot be built this way, and neither can `\"abcabcab\"`, because no piece repeats a whole number of times to fill it exactly.","constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 1e4","`s` has only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["The repeated block must be a prefix of s, and its length must divide s.length.","Try each divisor length d < n and check whether s equals its first d characters repeated.","A neat trick: s is made of a repeated block exactly when s appears in (s + s) with the first and last characters removed. The KMP prefix table gives an O(n) check too."],"explain":"\"abab\" is \"ab\" written twice, so the answer is `true`."},
{"slug":"repeated-string-match","title":"Repeated String Match","level":"Medium","summary":"Return the fewest times a must be repeated so that b is a substring of the result, or -1 if impossible.","method":"repeatedStringMatch","params":[["String","a"],["String","b"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["\"abcd\"","\"cdabcdab\""],"out":"3"},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aa\""],"out":"2"},{"in":["\"abc\"","\"wxyz\""],"out":"-1"},{"in":["\"abc\"","\"cabcabca\""],"out":"4"},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaab\"","\"ba\""],"out":"2"},{"in":["\"aaab\"","\"aabba\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"aaaaa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"ca\"","\"cab\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbaaa\"","\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"ac\"","\"caa\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"bbbabb\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaccbb\"","\"bb\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aaaaaaa\""],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["\"aabba\"","\"abbbbbabab\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"cc\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"bb\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\"","\"b\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"ac\"","\"bb\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"b\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"aaaaaaaa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"aaabaa\"","\"aaaabaaaaabaaaaaba\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"bbc\"","\"a\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaba\"","\"abaaabaaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"a\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bca\"","\"abcabcabc\""],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["\"caabab\"","\"abcaa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\"","\"aa\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\"","\"aaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\"","\"baba\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"b\"","\"cab\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"cbbc\"","\"a\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aaaa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"baca\"","\"abacabaca\""],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\"","\"aaa\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"a\"","\"aaabcaa\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"a\""],"out":"-1","g":1},{"in":["\"abcba\"","\"baabcba\""],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["\"bbb\"","\"bb\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"c\"","\"c\""],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaa\"","\"bbaabbaa\""],"out":"2","g":1}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"Return the minimum number of times you must repeat string `a` so that `b` becomes a substring of the result. If no number of repetitions works, return `-1`.\n\nRepeating `\"abc\"` 0 times gives `\"\"`, once gives `\"abc\"`, and twice gives `\"abcabc\"`.","constraints":["1 <= a.length, b.length <= 1e4","Both strings have only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Any match of b must start inside the first copy of a.","So you need at least ceil(b.length / a.length) copies, and never more than one extra copy beyond that.","Build the repeated string with q copies and check for b; if that fails, try q + 1; otherwise the answer is −1. Rabin–Karp or KMP make the search linear."],"explain":"Two copies \"abcdabcd\" do not contain \"cdabcdab\", but three copies \"abcdabcdabcd\" do (starting at index 2). So the answer is 3."},
{"slug":"repeated-dna-sequences","title":"Repeated DNA Sequences","level":"Medium","summary":"Return every 10-letter substring that occurs more than once in the DNA string, in any order.","method":"findRepeatedDnaSequences","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"List<String>","check":"any-order","tests":[{"in":["\"AAAAACCCCCAAAAACCCCCCAAAAAGGGTTT\""],"out":"[\"AAAAACCCCC\",\"CCCCCAAAAA\"]"},{"in":["\"AAAAAAAAAAAAA\""],"out":"[\"AAAAAAAAAA\"]"},{"in":["\"ACGT\""],"out":"[]"},{"in":["\"AAAAAAAAAAA\""],"out":"[\"AAAAAAAAAA\"]"},{"in":["\"GGGGGGG\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AACAAAAAAA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"A\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AACCCCAACCACAAAACCACCACCACCACACCCCACAAACACAAC\""],"out":"[\"ACCACCACCA\",\"CCACCACCAC\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"C\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TTTTTTT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GAC\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGG\""],"out":"[\"GGGGGGGGGG\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"TCAATCAATCAATCAATCAATCAATCAATAAATCAATCAATC\""],"out":"[\"TCAATCAATC\",\"CAATCAATCA\",\"ATCAATCAAT\",\"AATCAATCAA\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"AAAAA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC\""],"out":"[\"CCCCCCCCCC\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"AGC\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"ACAAGGAAGCA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTTT\""],"out":"[\"TTTTTTTTTT\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"AAA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"ACTCAC\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TCTATCT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGAGGGGGGG\""],"out":"[\"GGGGGGGGGG\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"TAAGCCATTC\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GAGGGAGAG\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TCGACGTGTCGGTTTTGTGAATTCCCCGTGTTAGAGCTAAGCGCACCTTCGCA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AAAAAAA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TGT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"G\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GACG\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GTAGGAGACGCCCCTAAGCCTCCGACGCGCTCGCA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AG\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"ATTTATTT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"CGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGTCCGT\""],"out":"[\"CGTCCGTCCG\",\"TCCGTCCGTC\",\"CCGTCCGTCC\",\"GTCCGTCCGT\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"AAAAAAAA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"CAAACCACCCCAAAAAAACAACCAAACCAACACACCACCACA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AAGAAA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"AT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"CCT\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"TCTCTCTC\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAGAG\""],"out":"[\"GAGAGAGAGA\",\"AGAGAGAGAG\"]","g":1},{"in":["\"AGCGA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":["\"GGAGA\""],"out":"[]","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#58124:236b5af26b2d6f90\"","perf":{"label":"a 100,000-letter DNA string","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(100000, \"ACGT\");"},"refMs":22}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"A DNA sequence is a string of the letters `A`, `C`, `G` and `T`. Return every 10-letter-long substring that occurs more than once in `s`.\n\nReturn each such substring once, in any order.\n\nSlide a 10-letter window along `s` and remember the windows you have already seen; a window seen a second time is part of the answer.","constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 1e5","`s` has only the letters A, C, G and T"],"hints":["Slide a window of length 10 and count the substrings you have seen.","A HashSet of seen substrings plus a set of repeated ones is simple and fast enough.","To save memory, encode each letter as 2 bits: a window is a 20-bit integer you can update in O(1) with a shift, an OR and a mask (a rolling hash)."],"explain":"\"AAAAACCCCC\" appears at index 0 and again at index 10, and \"CCCCCAAAAA\" appears at index 5 and index 15. No other 10-letter piece repeats, so the answer is `[\"AAAAACCCCC\",\"CCCCCAAAAA\"]`."},
{"slug":"longest-happy-prefix","title":"Longest Happy Prefix","level":"Hard","summary":"Return the longest non-empty proper prefix of s that is also a suffix (overlaps allowed), or \"\".","method":"longestPrefix","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"String","tests":[{"in":["\"level\""],"out":"\"l\""},{"in":["\"ababab\""],"out":"\"abab\""},{"in":["\"a\""],"out":"\"\""},{"in":["\"aaaa\""],"out":"\"aaa\""},{"in":["\"abcd\""],"out":"\"\""},{"in":["\"baabbabaabbbb\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaaabb\""],"out":"\"bb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cc\""],"out":"\"c\"","g":1},{"in":["\"b\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cbbbcbababbacaaabaacbacbc\""],"out":"\"c\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaababbbaaabaababaabbaa\""],"out":"\"bbaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbb\""],"out":"\"bb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"c\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"babbabbab\""],"out":"\"babbab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ababbbaababbbabaaabaaaab\""],"out":"\"ab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"caa\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbcbbc\""],"out":"\"bbc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbab\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cabbbbacbaabcbbcbacab\""],"out":"\"cab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbaccba\""],"out":"\"ccba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbbbbb\""],"out":"\"bbbbbbbbbb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aba\""],"out":"\"a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cccbbba\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"caaaaaabccb\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabaabaabaabaabaa\""],"out":"\"aabaabaabaabaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaccaaccc\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bba\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baabbabbbb\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abba\""],"out":"\"a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaba\""],"out":"\"a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"\"a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baabaabaabaabaabaabaabaabaab\""],"out":"\"baabaabaabaabaabaabaabaab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbc\""],"out":"\"cbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbcbc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbabbba\""],"out":"\"bba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaabbaaba\""],"out":"\"a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\""],"out":"\"aa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"babaaaba\""],"out":"\"ba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ccbccb\""],"out":"\"ccb\"","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#2:7cc7607b4949e25\"","perf":{"label":"a 100,000-character string","gen":"String a0 = \"a\".repeat(99999) + \"b\";"},"refMs":5}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"A happy prefix is a non-empty prefix of `s` that is also a suffix of `s`, not counting `s` itself. The prefix and the suffix may overlap.\n\nReturn the longest happy prefix, or `\"\"` if there is none.\n\nThis is exactly the last value of the KMP failure (prefix) function for `s`, so it can be found in linear time.","constraints":["1 <= s.length <= 1e5","`s` has only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Checking every length with a string comparison is O(n²).","This is exactly what the KMP prefix function computes: the length of the longest proper prefix that is also a suffix.","Build the prefix table for the whole string; the answer is s.substring(0, table[n − 1]). A rolling hash comparing prefix and suffix hashes also works."],"explain":"\"l\" is both the first and the last letter. Longer prefixes (\"le\", \"lev\", \"leve\") do not match the suffixes of the same length (\"el\", \"vel\", \"evel\"), so the answer is \"l\"."},
{"slug":"shortest-palindrome","title":"Shortest Palindrome","level":"Hard","summary":"Add the fewest characters in front of s to make it a palindrome, and return that palindrome.","method":"shortestPalindrome","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"String","tests":[{"in":["\"aacecaaa\""],"out":"\"aaacecaaa\""},{"in":["\"abcd\""],"out":"\"dcbabcd\""},{"in":["\"\""],"out":"\"\""},{"in":["\"a\""],"out":"\"a\""},{"in":["\"abab\""],"out":"\"babab\""},{"in":["\"bbbcaacbbbab\""],"out":"\"babbbcaacbbbab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"b\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"caa\""],"out":"\"aacaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbabbababbababbbbb\""],"out":"\"bbbbbababbababbabbababbababbbbb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ab\""],"out":"\"bab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cc\""],"out":"\"cc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbbb\""],"out":"\"bbbbbabbbbb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abbbba\""],"out":"\"abbbba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"\"aa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abb\""],"out":"\"bbabb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbbbbbab\""],"out":"\"babbbbbbbab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"c\""],"out":"\"c\"","g":1},{"in":["\"acbbaaca\""],"out":"\"acaabbcacbbaaca\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ba\""],"out":"\"aba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cabbccbbac\""],"out":"\"cabbccbbac\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cbbab\""],"out":"\"babbcbbab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baaa\""],"out":"\"aaabaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cacbbabacaabaabac\""],"out":"\"cabaabaacababbcacbbabacaabaabac\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"babba\""],"out":"\"abbabba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaab\""],"out":"\"baaaaab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"babbbbaaab\""],"out":"\"baaabbbbabbbbaaab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ababbabbabbaaabbaaab\""],"out":"\"baaabbaaabbabbabbababbabbabbaaabbaaab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bacaac\""],"out":"\"caacabacaac\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabb\""],"out":"\"bbaabb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baababbbbabaababa\""],"out":"\"ababaababbbbabaababa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baab\""],"out":"\"baab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabaaba\""],"out":"\"abaabaaba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaca\""],"out":"\"acabbaca\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\""],"out":"\"aaa\"","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#75002:36236506721ab2ef\"","perf":{"label":"a 50,000-character string","gen":"String a0 = \"a\".repeat(25000) + \"b\" + \"a\".repeat(24999);"},"refMs":12}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"You may add characters only in front of `s`. Return the shortest palindrome you can make this way.\n\nFor example \"abcd\" has only \"a\" as a palindromic start, so the answer there is \"dcbabcd\". Finding the longest palindromic prefix quickly is the heart of the problem.","constraints":["0 <= s.length <= 5e4","`s` has only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["Find the longest prefix of s that is already a palindrome. Only the rest needs to be mirrored in front.","The longest palindromic prefix is the longest prefix of s that equals a suffix of reverse(s).","Run the KMP prefix function on s + \"#\" + reverse(s). The last value is that length L; the answer is reverse(s.substring(L)) + s."],"explain":"The longest palindrome at the start of \"aacecaaa\" is \"aacecaa\". Only the final \"a\" is left over, so putting one \"a\" in front gives \"aaacecaaa\"."},
{"slug":"longest-duplicate-substring","title":"Longest Duplicate Substring","level":"Hard","summary":"Return any longest substring that occurs at least twice in s (occurrences may overlap), or \"\" if none.","method":"longestDupSubstring","params":[["String","s"]],"returns":"String","check":"custom:duplicateSubstring","tests":[{"in":["\"banana\""],"out":"\"ana\""},{"in":["\"abcd\""],"out":"\"\""},{"in":["\"aa\""],"out":"\"a\""},{"in":["\"abcabcab\""],"out":"\"abcab\""},{"in":["\"nnpxouomcofdjuujloanjimymadkuepightrfodmauhrsy\""],"out":"\"ma\""},{"in":["\"acabccccb\""],"out":"\"ccc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bab\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbaab\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bacbcbbaccaacbaabbccaababb\""],"out":"\"ccaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbb\""],"out":"\"bb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bccaaabaacccbaabccbaca\""],"out":"\"ccba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bnbabnba\""],"out":"\"bnba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"nn\""],"out":"\"n\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbabbabbabba\""],"out":"\"bbabbabba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bba\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaanaa\""],"out":"\"aa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bb\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aannaannaannaannaannannn\""],"out":"\"aannaannaannaanna\"","g":1},{"in":["\"caaacbcaaaabbaac\""],"out":"\"caaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ccccc\""],"out":"\"cccc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cccaccb\""],"out":"\"cc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaaaaaaaa\""],"out":"\"aaaaaaaaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"fkmjfmkfmmmmjmfkkmfjfkjm\""],"out":"\"mmm\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baabaabaabaa\""],"out":"\"baabaabaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ca\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaaa\""],"out":"\"aaa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"zj\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"nnnnnnnnnnnn\""],"out":"\"nnnnnnnnnnn\"","g":1},{"in":["\"anananananananananananana\""],"out":"\"ananananananananananana\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abb\""],"out":"\"b\"","g":1},{"in":["\"bbbb\""],"out":"\"bbb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabbaababbaabb\""],"out":"\"abbaab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"abc\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"nbnnbnnbnn\""],"out":"\"nbnnbnn\"","g":1},{"in":["\"babab\""],"out":"\"bab\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cc\""],"out":"\"c\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ababa\""],"out":"\"aba\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cb\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aaa\""],"out":"\"aa\"","g":1},{"in":["\"ccccacccbbabcacbabbbaccbbbc\""],"out":"\"ccbb\"","g":1},{"in":["\"aabb\""],"out":"\"a\"","g":1},{"in":["\"cccbcaaabaaaccabcbbccabcaaaa\""],"out":"\"ccabc\"","g":1},{"in":["\"sfesokit\""],"out":"\"s\"","g":1},{"in":["\"zfhqg\""],"out":"\"\"","g":1},{"in":["\"baccbc\""],"out":"\"c\"","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#1:af63a84c86019430\"","perf":{"label":"a 30,000-character string (length compared)","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(30000, \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\");","call":"Object r = s.longestDupSubstring(a0).length();"},"refMs":293}],"lesson":"string-matching","statement":"Return any longest substring of `s` that occurs at least twice (the occurrences may overlap). If no substring repeats, return `\"\"`.\n\nIf several repeated substrings have the maximum length, any of them is accepted.","constraints":["2 <= s.length <= 3e4","`s` has only lowercase English letters"],"hints":["If some substring of length L repeats, a substring of every shorter length repeats too. Binary-search the length.","To test a length L, slide a window over s with a rolling hash (Rabin–Karp) and look for a repeated hash.","Hash collisions can happen: confirm a match by comparing the actual substrings, or use two independent hashes. A suffix array also solves it."],"explain":"\"ana\" appears at index 1 and again at index 3 (the two copies overlap). No substring of length 4 appears twice, so the answer is \"ana\"."}
